==English==
{{wikipedia|Balsam (disambiguation)}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|balsem|balsum|balsome}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|balsamum}}, from {{der|en|grc|βάλσαμον|t=balsam}}, of {{der|en|sem}} origin ({{der|en|he|בושם||spice, perfume}}); compare {{cog|ang|balsam}}, {{m|ang|balsamum|t=balsam, balm}}, {{doublet|en|balm}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{enPR|bôlʹsəm}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈbɔːlsəm/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-balsam.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|UK}} A sweet-smelling [[oil]] or [[resin]] derived from various plants.
# {{lb|en|chiefly|UK}} A plant or tree yielding such substance.
# {{lb|en|chiefly|UK}} A [[soothing]] [[ointment]].
# {{lb|en|chiefly|UK|figuratively}} Something soothing.
#: ''Classical music is a sweet '''balsam''' for our sorrows''
# A [[flower]]ing plant of the genus ''[[Impatiens]]''.
# The balsam family of flowering plants ([[Balsaminaceae]]), which includes ''[[Impatiens]]'' and {{taxlink|Hydrocera|genus}}.
# A [[balsam fir]] ''[[Abies balsamea]]''.
# [[Canada balsam]], a turpentine obtained from the resin of balsam fir.

